Day 46: The Great Silence | Holy Saturday (Waiting for Resurrection)

📌 YouTube Description
Today the world goes quiet.
The stone is rolled into place.
And love waits in the dark.

Welcome to Day 46 of our Lenten journey, the stillness of Holy Saturday — the day suspended between death and life, sorrow and joy, endings and beginnings. This is the great silence, the day when nothing seems to move and yet everything is being transformed in the depths.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you into the mystery of waiting with God — trusting Him in the in‑between, in the unanswered prayers, in the quiet places where hope is learning to breathe again. Holy Saturday is not abandonment. It is hidden work. It is quiet victory. It is the dawn before the dawn.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Holy Saturday is a day of silence, waiting, and hidden hope

How God works in the depths even when nothing seems to be happening

Why waiting with God is never wasted

A prayer to trust God in the quiet and prepare for resurrection

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, I wait with You.”

